===Prohibited combinations===
Combinations that are regarded as a {{lang|de|Verstoß gegen die guten Sitten}}, which means "offence to moral and customs", are disallowed or otherwise avoided.<ref name="FZV" />{{rp|§9(1)}} This refers mostly to abbreviations relating to [[Nazi Germany]], such as ''NS'' ([[Nazism|National Socialism]]), ''KZ'' ({{lang|de|Konzentrationslager}}, [[Internment|concentration camp]]), ''HJ'' ({{lang|de|Hitlerjugend}}, [[Hitler Youth]]), ''SS'' ([[Schutzstaffel]]) and ''SA'' ([[Sturmabteilung]]). Therefore, these two-letter combinations are generally not issued in any district, nor do the city districts of [[Hanover]], [[Nuremberg]], [[Cologne]] and [[Stuttgart]] issue one-letter plates which would result in the combinations H-J, N-S, K-Z, S-A, S-D and S-S.<ref>{{cite web |title=Wunschkennzeichen |url=https://online-service2.nuernberg.de/wkz/controller;jsessionid=D245C32F7CEB5A745BBB2021A885B44A |website=Stadt Nürnberg Ordnungsamt |publisher=City of Nuremberg |access-date=2020-12-30 |language=de}}</ref><ref name="Köln">{{cite web |title=Wunschkennzeichen – Stadt Köln |url=http://www.stadt-koeln.de/service/produkt/wunschkennzeichen?kontrast=weiss |website=Stadt Köln |publisher=City of Cologne |access-date=2020-12-30 |location=• Spezielle und verbotene Kennzeichen |language=de}}</ref><ref name="Stuttgart">{{cite web |title=Kraftfahrzeugkennzeichen – Wunschkennzeichen reservieren |date=6 June 2025 |url=https://www.stuttgart.de/organigramm/leistungen/kraftfahrzeugkennzeichen-wunschkennzeichen-reservieren |publisher=City of Stuttgart |access-date=2025-07-31 |language=de}}</ref>

[[File:Straßenwacht vom Allgemeinen Deutschen Automobil-Club e.V. (ADAC) (Kiel 36.733).jpg|thumb|right|ADAC car parade in 1965 – the plate on the far left reads M-SA 617]]
Those prefixes must not be issued as middle letters now, yet the list of forbidden codes appears to have developed over the decades. In the 1960s, the renowned [[ADAC]] had no qualms with the middle letters ''SA'', as seen on an archive photo. Although the "infamous" combinations were generally excluded from the list of possible area codes with the introduction of the current system, the French occupation force had between 1945 and 1949 used the combination '''SA''' followed by the double-digit numbers 01 to 08 for the then seven rural districts in the [[Saar (protectorate)|Saar Protectorate]] and its capital [[Saarbrücken]]. By 1990, however, codes like these were not taken into consideration for newly formed districts in former GDR: The district {{lang|de|[[Sächsische Schweiz]]}} used the name of its capital, [[Pirna]], in its code '''PIR''', to avoid the use of ''SS''. When the districts of [[Torgau]], [[Delitzsch]] and [[Oschatz]] merged into {{lang|de|[[Nordsachsen]]}}, they combined their initials into '''TDO''', instead of abbreviating ''Northern Saxony'' as ''NS''.{{efn|TOD would have seemed indecent too, as it means ''death''.}}

[[File:Deutsches Kfz-Kennzeichen mit Erkennungsnummer NS.jpg|thumb|200px|right|Example of banned combination ([[Nazism|NS]]) which was issued accidentally]]
On the other hand, the area codes '''HH''' and '''AH''' were chosen for {{lang|de|Hansestadt Hamburg}} and former district {{lang|de|[[Ahaus]]}}, although they could be interpreted as {{lang|de|[[Nazi salute|Heil Hitler]]}} and {{lang|de|[[Adolf Hitler]]}}, respectively. In everyday German, the letters AH are not regarded as an obvious abbreviation for that name,{{efn|AH would rather be regarded as an abbreviation for {{lang|de|Altenheim}} (old people's home) or {{lang|de|Autohaus}} (car dealership); cf. [[:de:AH|German Wikipedia]].}} even less so in the 1950s when the lists were created.{{efn|It was certainly not common to refer to the Nazi {{lang|de|"Führer"}} by his initials, neither before nor after 1945.}} Nonetheless, these two-letter codes and the respective numerals 18 and 88, signifying the first and eighth letter of the alphabet, obviously have developed into [[Nazi symbolism|Nazi symbols]]. They are therefore generally avoided in the serial part of licence plates, although they may be found sometimes.<ref>{{cite news|title=M-AH 8888 ist durchgerutscht|trans-title=M-AH 8888 slipped through|url=http://www.sueddeutsche.de/muenchen/behoerdenfehler-m-ah-ist-durchgerutscht-1.2683534|language=de|work=[[Sueddeutsche Zeitung]]|date=2015-10-09|access-date=2015-10-09}}</ref> Generally, the decision whether or not a certain combination is permitted lies with the respective district authority. In Brandenburg, any plates that are related to Hitler, the Hitler salute, etc. cannot be issued, especially if they would be bearing digits 1888, 8818, 8888 or ending in 88, 888, 188. Nor can the combinations AH&nbsp;18 and HH&nbsp;18 be issued to new owners.<ref>{{cite news|title=Verschärfte Regeln gegen Nazi-Autokennzeichen|trans-title=Stricter rules against Nazi plates|url=http://www.rp-online.de/panorama/deutschland/verschaerfte-regeln-gegen-nazi-autokennzeichen-aid-1.2003785|work=Rheinische Post|date=2010-09-18|language=de}}</ref> Some districts however allow these combinations if they are the owner's initials (for example, {{lang|de|Norbert Schmidt}} might be able to get XX-NS&nbsp;1234).{{citation needed|date=January 2021}}

In 2004 in [[Nuremberg]], a car owner was refused a number plate beginning ''N-PD'' because of the connection to the political party [[National Democratic Party of Germany|NPD]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Nicht erlaubt – Hinter diesen Kfz-Kennzeichen stecken Nazi-Codes|trans-title=Not allowed – these licence plates conceal nazi codes|url=http://www.mopo.de/ratgeber/auto-mobil/nicht-erlaubt-hinter-diesen-kfz-kennzeichen-stecken-nazi-codes-986986|work=[[Hamburger Morgenpost]]|date=2015-04-23|access-date=2020-04-08|language=de}}</ref> After the terror group [[National Socialist Underground]] was uncovered in 2011, the city of [[Nuremberg]] refused number plates beginning with ''N-SU'' and even abolished the respective plates on their own vehicles of {{lang|de|Stadtentwässerung und Umweltanalytik}} (sewage and environmental department).<ref>{{cite news|title=Nürnberg entfernt NSU-Kennzeichen|trans-title=Nuremberg removes NSU plates|url=http://www.nordbayern.de/region/nuernberg/nurnberg-entfernt-nsu-kennzeichen-1.2493976|work=[[Nürnberger Nachrichten]]|date=2012-11-09|access-date=2020-04-08|language=de}}</ref>
In the 2010s, some districts started banning licence plates with the middle letters IS which resembled the [[Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant|Islamic State]].<ref>{{cite news |title=IS als Auto-Kennzeichen verbieten? |trans-title=Forbidding IS as a licence plate? |url=http://www.fr.de/frankfurt/islamischer-staat-org187056/auto-kennzeichen-verbieten-11116839.html |work=[[Frankfurter Rundschau]] |date=2016-04-22|language=de}}</ref> The [[Herford (district)|Herford]] district registration office ceased issuing registration plates with the combination HF-Z in April 2022 to avoid connotations with the use of the letter "[[Z (military symbol)|Z]]" as a symbol for the [[2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Keine "Z"-Kennzeichen mehr im Kreis Herford |trans-title=No more "Z" license plates in the Herford district |url=https://www1.wdr.de/nachrichten/westfalen-lippe/keine-z-nummernschilder-im-kreis-herford-100.html |access-date=2023-02-04 |website=WDR |date=2022-04-08 |language=de}}</ref>

[[File:Aken.jpg|thumb|right|Permitted: [[Aachen|AC]]-AB]]
The combinations [[Starnberg (district)|STA]]-SI, [[Stuttgart|S]]-ED<ref name=Stuttgart />/[[Segeberg|SE]]-D,<ref name=Segeberg>{{cite web |title=Wunschkennzeichen |url=https://www.segeberg.de/Lebenslagen/Klima-Wirtschaft-Verkehr/Wunschkennzeichen/ |website=Kreis Segeberg |publisher=Kraftfahrzeug-Zulassungsbehörde |access-date=2024-07-26 |language=de }}</ref> [[Helmstedt (district)|HE]]-IL/[[Dithmarschen|HEI]]-L, [[Steinburg|IZ]]-AN and [[Warendorf|WAF]]-FE are also forbidden or discouraged, to avoid association with [[Stasi]], the {{lang|de|[[Socialist Unity Party of Germany|Sozialistische Einheitspartei]]}} of the GDR, the [[Nazi salute]], NAZI backwards and the German word for weapon respectively<!-- ref German Wp -->. Other combinations affected are [[Burglengenfeld|BUL]]-LE (German derogative for police, roughly comparable to ''pig''),<ref>{{cite news |title=Autokennzeichen "BUL-LE" aus dem Verkehr gezogen |trans-title=Car plate sign "BUL-LE" withdrawn from circulation |url=https://www.welt.de/regionales/muenchen/article118973436/Autokennzeichen-BUL-LE-aus-dem-Verkehr-gezogen.html |work=Die Welt |date=2013-08-13 |language=de}}</ref> [[Moers|MO]]-RD (German word for murder),<ref>{{cite news |title=30 Moerser wollten Kennzeichen MO-RD |trans-title=30 Moers people wanted plate "MO-RD" |url=http://www.rp-online.de/nrw/staedte/moers/30-moerser-wollten-kennzeichen-mo-rd-aid-1.3066626 |work=Rheinische Post |date=2012-11-13| language=de}}</ref> [[Nordsachsen|TO]]-D (German word for death), [[Kiel|KI]]-LL (kill) and [[Siegburg|SU]]-FF (boozing).<ref>{{cite news |title=Lieber kein SU-FF für Autofahrer |trans-title=Rather no SU-FF ''(booze)'' for automobilists |url=https://www.broeltal.de/nachrichten/artikel/lieber-kein-su-ff-fuer-autofahrer.html |access-date=2020-12-30 |agency=broeltal.de |date=2016-05-10 |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Wunschkennzeichen |website=Rhein-Sieg-Kreis |url=https://igv-kfz.regioit.de/verkehr-igv/servlet/Internetgeschaeftsvorfaelle?AUFRUF=WKZ_RSK |language=de |access-date=2024-07-26}}</ref>

[[File:SEX146 licence plate of Kreis Segeberg.JPG|thumb|right|Consensual: [[Segeberg|SE]]-X]]
On the other hand, plates that would seem offensive in other circumstances have been allowed, such as the infamous acronym [[Acab|AC-AB]]. Since the 1950s, morals and customs have certainly changed, and combinations which may have appeared indecent then do not raise an eyebrow now. Therefore, it is not a problem to get a licence plate with S-EX,<ref name=Stuttgart /> SE-X or SE-XY,<ref name=Segeberg /> for example.

===Reserved combinations===
[[File:Kfz-Kennzeichen Polizei Sachsen.jpg|thumb|right|Licence plate of a police car in Saxony]]
For quite different reasons, some districts hold certain letter combinations reserved. The Saxon capital [[Dresden]] issues all '''DD-Q''' plates to the state police vehicles. Likewise, [[Erfurt]] uses '''EF-LP''' for the police in Thuringia. [[Munich]] and other Bavarian cities reserve certain combinations with ''P'' for the police units within their [[Bavarian State Police#Organization|authorities]], such as '''[[Munich|M]]-PM''', '''[[Nuremberg|N]]-PP''' or '''[[Rosenheim|RO]]-P'''.<ref>{{cite web |title=Wie sehen Polizeikennzeichen aus? |trans-title=What do police plates look like? |url=http://autokennzeichen.de/polizeikennzeichen/ |website=Autokennzeichen.de |date=2017-08-03 |access-date=2020-12-30 |language=de}}</ref> Cologne issues '''K-TX''' to taxis and '''K-LN''' to the city's own vehicles.<ref name="Köln" /> In various districts, firefighter vehicles will be issued the middle letters '''FW''' standing for {{lang|de|Feuerwehr}}.<ref>{{cite news |last=Feuerwehr [[Essen]] |first=(Essen Fire Dept.) |title=FW-E: Feuerwehrfahrzeuge mit neuen KFZ-Kennzeichen unterwegs |trans-title=Fire Engines on the road with new number plates |url=https://www.presseportal.de/blaulicht/pm/56893/958176 |language=de |access-date=2021-06-20 |date=2007-03-20}}</ref> The combinations '''B-FA''' and '''BN-AA''' with any 4-digit numbers are issued by Berlin and Bonn, respectively, to embassy domestic staff without diplomatic status.<ref name="KW-Diplo" />

===Fictitious licence plates===
[[File:German license plate.svg|thumb|right|An example of a fake number plate, seemingly from Munich but obviously not correct, due to the umlaut and the leading digit 0]]
Sometimes, such as in films or television series, it may be necessary to show licence plates which do not really belong to any vehicle. The easiest way would be to create a fictional area code, such as ''NN-XY 555''. In the 1980s TV series {{lang|de|[[Der Fahnder]]}},<ref>[https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0088517/ ''Der Fahnder'' on IMDb]</ref> the area code '''G''' was used for a fictional "large city" ({{langx|de|'''G'''roßstadt}}) in the [[Ruhrgebiet]] area. However, if the plot is supposed to take place in a defined town or region, the audience would expect cars to show codes of that area on their number plates. When James Bond was driving through Hamburg in ''[[Tomorrow Never Dies]]'', the obviously fake Berlin licence plates on his BMW were soon pointed out.<ref>{{cite web |title=Auto-Filmfehler bei James Bond |trans-title=Car-Filmbugs at James Bond |url=http://www.autobild.de/bilder/auto-filmfehler-bei-james-bond-6719669.html#bild5 |publisher=Auto Bild |access-date=2020-12-24 |language=de |archive-date=26 September 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180926121826/http://www.autobild.de/bilder/auto-filmfehler-bei-james-bond-6719669.html#bild5 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Prior to 2000, it was also possible to use number plates with bogus identifiers containing the letters B, F, G, I, O and Q, which at that time were not issued in the middle group.  However, any of these letters can appear on a real licence plate. In order to demonstrate clearly that the plate shown is a fictitious one, the crew could use an impossible identifier, such as an {{lang|de|umlaut}} in this middle section.

==Registration==
===Procedures===
[[File:Schildershop.jpg|thumb|right|Several shops advertising {{lang|de|Schilder}} (plates), in the street of the registration authority]]
Vehicles must be registered with their owner's name and current address. On proof of identity, vehicle documentation and liability insurance, the registration will take place in the [[districts of Germany|district]] authority competent for the respective address.<ref name="FZV" />{{rp|§6}} An alphanumeric combination, which can be reserved according to personal wishes, will be issued to the vehicle. The physical plates, however, have to be acquired separately, either at a local store or online.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://autoschild-kaufen.de/blog/kennzeichen-kosten/ |title=Das kosten Kennzeichen |date=2019-05-29 |trans-title=This is what plates cost |access-date=2020-10-29 |language=de}}</ref> Both the dimensions of the plates and the typeface of letters and numbers are standardized. After purchasing the number plate, the official stamps must be applied, back at the registration office.<ref name="FZV" />{{rp|§12(3)}} A fee is payable for the registration, in addition to the expenses for the plates.

Any registration or change of it will be registered both within the district authority and nationwide. The latter task is carried out by the Central Vehicle Register ({{lang|de|Zentrales Fahrzeugregister}}, ZFZR) which is controlled by the Federal Motor Transport Authority ({{lang|de|Kraftfahrt-Bundesamt}}, KBA).<ref name=ZFZR>{{Cite web |title=Straßenverkehrsgesetz |url=https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/stvg/__31.html |publisher=Bundesamt für Justiz |date=2024-07-12 |access-date=2024-07-27 |language=de}}</ref>{{rp|§31}} The data which are stored there refer to the vehicle, the owner and the insurance.<ref name=ZFZR />{{rp|§33}}<ref>{{cite web |title=Central Vehicle Register |url=https://www.kba.de/EN/Themen_en/ZentraleRegister_en/ZFZR_en/zfzr_node_en.html |publisher=Kraftfahrt-Bundesamt |access-date=2024-08-09 |language=en}}</ref> Inquiries from foreign authorities can be addressed to ZFZR which will then direct them to the correct district.<ref name=ZFZR />{{rp|§37}}<ref>{{cite web |title=EUCARIS |url=https://www.kba.de/EN/Themen_en/ZentraleRegister_en/EUCARIS_en/eucaris_node_en.html |publisher=Kraftfahrt-Bundesamt |access-date=2024-08-09 |language=en |quote=Cross-border prosecution of traffic violations}}</ref>

Changes, such as a vehicle being sold or its owner moving residence, must be registered to keep the vehicle documentation up to date.<ref name="FZV" />{{rp|§15}} If the vehicle remains within the district, the licence plates may be retained. A vehicle being relocated outside of the district has to be registered at the authority now competent. Whilst it was mandatory to have the plates altered, according to the current address, this obligation was reduced in 2015 and has meanwhile been abolished. Since then, it is generally not possible any more to tell the owner's district of residence from the area code on the plates, as they may have registered it at a former residence e.g. in Hamburg yet moved to Frankfurt meanwhile.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.vz-nrw.de/energie-und-verkehr#kfzkennzeichenhhauchfuerfrankfurter |title=Kfz-Kennzeichen: HH auch für Frankfurter |access-date=2014-12-09 |author=Verbraucherzentrale Nordrhein-Westfalen e.V. |date=2014-12-02 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141209153728/http://www.vz-nrw.de/energie-und-verkehr#kfzkennzeichenhhauchfuerfrankfurter |archive-date=9 December 2014 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref>

[[File:Defacedgermanplate.JPG|thumb|right|Example of a defaced plate – notice how the bottom seal is completely gone, due to scraping. (from [[Kronach]]).]]
When owners choose to deregister their vehicle, the officer at the local authority will want to see the licence plates with defaced seals on them as proof that the plate can no longer be used in public. For this purpose, scratching tools are available for use at the registration office. Once defaced, the plates may only be used legally on public roads for one return journey to the owner's residence. If a vehicle is to be deregistered and a new one registered to the same owner, it is possible to swap the licence plate from old to new within the same process. Documentation and fees are necessary nonetheless, and neither vehicle should be used to reach the authority, as the assignment of the number changes by the minute.

It is general practice for owners to deregister their vehicles when selling them, typically when a sale is agreed. A sales contract is highly recommended, and various forms are available online for free.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.adac.de/rund-ums-fahrzeug/auto-kaufen-verkaufen/gebrauchtwagenkauf/kfz-kaufvertrag/ |title=Kaufvertrag fürs Auto |trans-title=Sales contract for the car |publisher=[[ADAC]] |access-date=2020-12-18 |language=de |date=2020-12-16}}</ref> A seller may hand over their vehicle with valid licence plates and papers still in their name to the new owner, and the owner will complete the registration transfer to their name. In a scenario without a proper sales contract, the seller may become liable when the buyer commits traffic violations or even criminal acts related to the car or plates. It is generally not recommended to sell used cars with licence plates.

A car whose owner has not paid their insurance premium and is reported to the police by the insurance company may get {{lang|de|entstempelt}}, ''unstamped'' when found in a public place. The police will remove the official seal using a scratching tool like a screwdriver, leaving the plate without a valid seal. This renders the vehicle illegal to be used, or to be left in a public place, unless the insurance premium is paid and plates are fitted with a new official seal. A one-time journey to the relevant registration authorities is permitted to have the seal reinstated, once insurance is restored.

===Costs===
As of 2020, the average registration fee is €26.00<ref>{{cite web |title=Gebührenordnung für Maßnahmen im Straßenverkehr |trans-title=Fees for measures in road traffic |url=http://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/stgebo_2011/GebOSt.pdf |website=Gesetze-im-Internet.de |pages=13–16 |language=de |publisher={{lang|de|Bundesministerium der Justiz}} (Federal Ministry of Justice) |date=2020-06-29 |access-date=2020-11-11}}</ref> whilst further fees may apply for choosing an individual identifier or for reservation of such. Whereas some of these amounts are ordained by federal laws, others vary slightly from one district to the next.<ref>{{cite news |title=Kfz Behörden Gebühren |url=http://www.strassenverkehrsamt.de/artikel/kfz-behoerden-gebuehren |access-date=2020-12-23 |publisher=Strassenverkehrsamt |language=de}}</ref> The prices for number plates, on the other hand, are subject to the free market and range from less than €10 up to around €40 per piece. Generally, it is cheaper to have the plates ordered online, but faster to walk across the street and have them made on the spot.

Further costs arise for [[Road tax#Germany|motor vehicle tax]] (€194 on average<ref>{{cite web |title=KFZ Steuer |url=http://kfzversicherungen.org/kfz-steuer/ |website=KfzVersicherungen.org |date=2015-09-15 |access-date=2021-01-02 |language=de}}</ref> yet very much depending on engine and emissions) and mandatory liability insurance (€260 on average, in 2019;<ref>{{cite web |title=Versicherungen |url=http://de.statista.com/statistik/daten/studie/156096/umfrage/durchschnittliche-jahrespraemie-in-der-kfz-haftpflichtversicherung/ |website=Statista |access-date=2021-01-02 |language=de |date=2020-09-24}}</ref> depending on the model of the vehicle, age and residence of the owner, etc.). [[Vehicle insurance#Germany|Comprehensive insurance]] is recommended but voluntary.

===Special types of registration===
Besides the most common way of registering a vehicle for everyday, all-year use indefinitely, it is possible to register for several months of each year, or for a few days in order to export the vehicle abroad. As well it is allowed, under certain restrictions, to register two vehicles (such as a car and a [[motorhome]]) under one number, with the same main licence plate. These variations may save expenses in tax and insurance. Further ways of saving apply to vintage cars and to electrically powered vehicles. Each of these special registrations are represented in the respective licence plate.

==Special codes, colours and formats==
Certain types of vehicle bear special codes.<ref name=FZV />{{rp|App. 3}}{{efn|Appendix 3 defines the unique prefixes for vehicles of federal and state government bodies, agencies, police, the armed forces, diplomatic missions and privileged international organizations.}}

===Different codes===
In deviating from the system described above, vehicles registered to federal, state or communal owners can bear licence plates not showing the district and sometimes omitting the middle letters.

====Highest state offices====
[[File:Licenseplate of limousine.png|thumb|200px|Plate of the German Chancellor]]
The [[President of Germany|President]] uses the licence plate '''0-1''', the [[Chancellor of Germany (Federal Republic)|Chancellor]] uses '''0-2''', the [[Minister for Foreign Affairs (Germany)|Foreign Minister]] uses '''0-3''' and the ''First [[Secretary of State#Germany|State Secretary]] of the [[Foreign Office (Germany)|Foreign Office]]'' (i.e. the deputy Foreign Minister) uses '''0-4'''. The [[President of the Bundestag|President of the Parliament]] uses '''1-1'''. This reflects the fact that the Parliament's president is not part of the executive branch but still ranks higher in (symbolic) importance than the Chancellor. These vehicles are tax-exempt and need not to be insured since the German government acts as insurer.

====Federal government====
[[File:Bundesfinanzverwaltung license plate of Germany.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|de|Bundesfinanzverwaltung}} (customs)]]
